# Castle Garenbrig's six {G} pay for an ability of a creature as its source was when the ability was activated (CR 602.2a,
# 113.7a), though the source stops being a creature while the cost is paid (CR 601.2g-h): it is the same object, changed
# in place.
# Mycosynth Lattice makes every permanent an artifact, so March of the Machines makes Aether Spellbomb - and March itself -
# artifact creatures (the lands and the last Mox, 0/0, die). Turn 7 the Castle's six {G} are made first; the Ironworks
# sacrifices two Moxen to cast March and the tapped Forest for {C}{C} more. Bot1 activates the Spellbomb's "{1}, Sacrifice
# this artifact: Draw a card", an ability of a creature: with {C} and restricted {G} in the pool it is asked what pays
# (CR 601.2g-h). It sacrifices March to Krark-Clan Ironworks first (a mana ability, CR 605.3a), so the Spellbomb, the same
# object, is no longer a creature, then pays the {1} with one of the Castle's {G}, not a {C}: the card is drawn, and four
# {C} and five {G} are left. (Read as the Spellbomb is when the {G} is spent, the {G} would not be offered.)

